  "notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental statement lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4). Taxes = Statement of Activities Property taxes (p2). Intergovernmental 192,379 split using the Statement of Activities general receipts (motor vehicle 65,435, sales and use 84,577, state aid 32,367, p2) with the 10,000 remainder (fire and rescue operating grant) kept as Intergovernmental; Grants and donations 132,675 split into operating grants 6,525, capital grants 124,829 and donations 1,321 (p2). Net interfund transfers (14,835) out of governmental funds to the Utilities fund. Fund balances (not cash) in the fund_balance fields; cash null. Business-type lines from the modified cash business-type statement (p6), which ties to the Statement of Activities (p2: disbursements 2,827,897; charges 177,777; capital grants 2,591,448; interest 1,720; transfers 14,835) and the budget schedule Utilities row (p7). No proprietary cash flow statement. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds balance sheet (p3; totals equal p1), business-type and totals from p1; p3 Total-column Restricted 172,885 recorded as printed (see report_discrepancies). Detail: the only supplementary schedule (p7) is a combined all-funds budget schedule, so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds statement (p4) and the business-type statement (p6). Read pages 1-7 of 7"
